  "relevance_note": "User-reported failure mode: multi-agent context inheritance causes instruction/identity conflicts and large context overhead; proposes explicit opt-out for project context injection.",
  "reason_included": "High-detail issue report capturing policy-layer failure (identity/authority confusion) and suggesting concrete contract fields (skip/context list).",
  "claim_snippets": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "claim_text": "The issue contrasts sub-agents and teammates: sub-agents appear to avoid the CLAUDE.md inheritance problem but have a reduced toolset compared with teammates.",
      "claim_status": "anecdotal"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "claim_text": "When spawning a teammate with a custom agent definition, the teammate loads both the agent MD file and the project's `CLAUDE.md`, which can create identity conflicts and waste context window.",
      "claim_status": "anecdotal"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "claim_text": "The issue reports there is no opt-out mechanism to load only the agent MD and skip `CLAUDE.md`; a workaround is to add a disambiguation block to every agent MD telling it to ignore `CLAUDE.md` identity instructions.",
      "claim_status": "anecdotal"
    }
  ],
